Article 2 (Special Cases concerning Applications for Extension of Validity Period of Excellent Enterprise Certification)
An enterprise for which less than 90 days remain in the validity period of its excellent enterprise certification as at the time this Decree enters into force may apply for extension of the certification validity period by the date on which the remaining validity period of its excellent enterprise certification expires, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 7 (5). In such cases, the excellent enterprise certification shall be deemed valid until the date on which a decision on extension of the certification validity period is made pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 7 (6).

Article 3 (Transitional Measures concerning Validity Period of Excellent Enterprise Certification)
Where the validity period of excellent enterprise certification has not expired as at the time this Decree enters into force, the former provisions shall apply, notwithstanding the amended provisions of the main clause of Article 7 (3); provided, where a new evaluation is undergone pursuant to the proviso of Article 7 (3) on or after the date this Decree enters into force, the certification validity period shall be four years from the date of certification following that evaluation, pursuant to the amended provisions of the main clause of Article 7 (3).

